#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:6
msgid "Attributes in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:12
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:14
msgid "This page lists the attributes currently supported by Clang."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:16
msgid "AArch64 SME Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:18
msgid ""
"Clang supports a number of AArch64-specific attributes to manage state added "
"by the Scalable Matrix Extension (SME). This state includes the runtime mode "
"that the processor is in (e.g. non-streaming or streaming) as well as the "
"state of the `ZA` Matrix Storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:23
msgid "The attributes come in the form of type- and declaration attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:25
msgid ""
"The SME declaration attributes can appear anywhere that a standard `[[...]]` "
"declaration attribute can appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:27
msgid ""
"The SME type attributes apply only to prototyped functions and can appear "
"anywhere that a standard `[[...]]` type attribute can appear. The SME type "
"attributes do not apply to functions having a K&R-style unprototyped "
"function type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:32
msgid ""
"See [Arm C Language Extensions](https://github.com/ARM-software/acle) for "
"more details about the features related to the SME extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:35
msgid ""
"See [Procedure Call Standard for the Arm® 64-bit Architecture (AArch64)]"
"(https://github.com/ARM-software/abi-aa) for more details about streaming-"
"interface functions and shared/private-ZA interface functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:38
msgid "__arm_agnostic"
msgstr ""

