#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:55
msgid "`__arm_agnostic`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:61
msgid ""
"The `__arm_agnostic` keyword applies to prototyped function types and "
"affects the function's calling convention for a given state S. This "
"attribute allows the user to describe a function that preserves S, without "
"requiring the function to share S with its callers and without making the "
"assumption that S exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:67
msgid ""
"If a function has the `__arm_agnostic(S)` attribute and calls a function "
"without this attribute, then the function's object code will contain code to "
"preserve state S. Otherwise, the function's object code will be the same as "
"if it did not have the attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:72
msgid ""
"The attribute takes string arguments to describe state S. The supported "
"states are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:75
msgid "`\"sme_za_state\"` for state enabled by PSTATE.ZA, such as ZA and ZT0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:77
msgid ""
"The attribute `__arm_agnostic(\"sme_za_state\")` cannot be used in "
"conjunction with `__arm_in(S)`, `__arm_out(S)`, `__arm_inout(S)` or "
"`__arm_preserves(S)` where state S describes state enabled by PSTATE.ZA, "
"such as \"za\" or \"zt0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:83
msgid "__arm_in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:100
msgid "`__arm_in`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:106
msgid ""
"The `__arm_in` keyword applies to prototyped function types and specifies "
"that the function shares a given state S with its caller. For `__arm_in`, "
"the function takes the state S as input and returns with the state S "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:110 ../../../AttributeReference.md:146
#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:266 ../../../AttributeReference.md:302
msgid ""
"The attribute takes string arguments to instruct the compiler which state is "
"shared. The supported states for S are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:113 ../../../AttributeReference.md:149
#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:223 ../../../AttributeReference.md:269
#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:305
msgid "`\"za\"` for Matrix Storage (requires SME)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:115 ../../../AttributeReference.md:151
#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:271 ../../../AttributeReference.md:307
msgid ""
"The attributes `__arm_in(S)`, `__arm_out(S)`, `__arm_inout(S)` and "
"`__arm_preserves(S)` are all mutually exclusive for the same state S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:119
msgid "__arm_inout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:136
msgid "`__arm_inout`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:142
msgid ""
"The `__arm_inout` keyword applies to prototyped function types and specifies "
"that the function shares a given state S with its caller. For `__arm_inout`, "
"the function takes the state S as input and returns new state for S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:155
msgid "__arm_locally_streaming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:172
msgid "`__arm_locally_streaming`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:178
msgid ""
"The `__arm_locally_streaming` keyword applies to function declarations and "
"specifies that all the statements in the function are executed in streaming "
"mode. This means that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:182 ../../../AttributeReference.md:227
msgid ""
"the function requires that the target processor implements the Scalable "
"Matrix Extension (SME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:184
msgid ""
"the program automatically puts the machine into streaming mode before "
"executing the statements and automatically restores the previous mode "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:188
msgid ""
"Clang manages PSTATE.SM automatically; it is not the source code's "
"responsibility to do this. For example, Clang will emit code to enable "
"streaming mode at the start of the function, and disable streaming mode at "
"the end of the function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:194
msgid "__arm_new"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:211
msgid "`__arm_new`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:217
msgid ""
"The `__arm_new` keyword applies to function declarations and specifies that "
"the function will create a new scope for state S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:220
msgid ""
"The attribute takes string arguments to instruct the compiler for which "
"state to create new scope. The supported states for S are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:225
msgid "For state `\"za\"`, this means that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:229
msgid "the function will commit any lazily saved ZA data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:230
msgid "the function will create a new ZA context and enable PSTATE.ZA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:231
msgid ""
"the function will disable PSTATE.ZA (by setting it to 0) before returning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:233
msgid ""
"For `__arm_new(\"za\")` functions Clang will set up the ZA context "
"automatically on entry to the function and disable it before returning. For "
"example, if ZA is in a dormant state Clang will generate the code to commit "
"a lazy-save and set up a new ZA state before executing user code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:239
msgid "__arm_out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:256
msgid "`__arm_out`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:262
msgid ""
"The `__arm_out` keyword applies to prototyped function types and specifies "
"that the function shares a given state S with its caller. For `__arm_out`, "
"the function ignores the incoming state for S and returns new state for S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:275
msgid "__arm_preserves"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:292
msgid "`__arm_preserves`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:298
msgid ""
"The `__arm_preserves` keyword applies to prototyped function types and "
"specifies that the function does not read a given state S and returns with "
"state S unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:311
msgid "__arm_streaming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:328
msgid "`__arm_streaming`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:334
msgid ""
"The `__arm_streaming` keyword applies to prototyped function types and "
"specifies that the function has a \"streaming interface\". This means that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:337
msgid ""
"the function requires that the processor implements the Scalable Matrix "
"Extension (SME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:339
msgid ""
"the function must be entered in streaming mode (that is, with PSTATE.SM set "
"to 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:341
msgid "the function must return in streaming mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:343
msgid ""
"Clang manages PSTATE.SM automatically; it is not the source code's "
"responsibility to do this. For example, if a non-streaming function calls an "
"`__arm_streaming` function, Clang generates code that switches into "
"streaming mode before calling the function and switches back to non-"
"streaming mode on return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:350
msgid "__arm_streaming_compatible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:367
msgid "`__arm_streaming_compatible`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:373
msgid ""
"The `__arm_streaming_compatible` keyword applies to prototyped function "
"types and specifies that the function has a \"streaming compatible "
"interface\". This means that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:377
msgid ""
"the function may be entered in either non-streaming mode (PSTATE.SM=0) or in "
"streaming mode (PSTATE.SM=1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:379
msgid "the function must return in the same mode as it was entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:380
msgid "the code executed in the function is compatible with either mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:382
msgid ""
"Clang manages PSTATE.SM automatically; it is not the source code's "
"responsibility to do this. Clang will ensure that the generated code in "
"streaming-compatible functions is valid in either mode (PSTATE.SM=0 or "
"PSTATE.SM=1). For example, if an `__arm_streaming_compatible` function calls "
"a non-streaming function, Clang generates code to temporarily switch out of "
"streaming mode before calling the function and switch back to streaming-mode "
"on return if `PSTATE.SM` is `1` on entry of the caller. If `PSTATE.SM` is "
"`0` on entry to the `__arm_streaming_compatible` function, the call will be "
"executed without changing modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:393
msgid "AMD GPU Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:397
msgid "amdgpu_av"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:410
msgid "`amdgpu_av`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:411 ../../../AttributeReference.md:412
msgid "`clang::amdgpu_av`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:420
msgid ""
"This attribute controls availability and visibility as described in the "
"[AMDGPU Memory Model](https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPUMemoryModel.html). When "
"placed on an atomic expression or fence, the resulting atomic or fence "
"instruction carries the corresponding *AV Metadata*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:425
msgid ""
"The attribute takes a string literal as an argument, which currently has "
"only one supported value:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:428
msgid ""
"`\"none\"`: Disable MakeAvailable and MakeVisible semantics on release and "
"acquire operations respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:441
msgid "amdgpu_flat_work_group_size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AttributeReference.md:454
msgid "`amdgpu_flat_work_group_size`"
msgstr ""

